NAME
       host - look up the IPv4 addresses of a host name

SYNOPSIS
       **host** __NAME__

DESCRIPTION
       Resolves __NAME__ the same way programs do: /etc/hosts first, then the
       DNS servers listed in /etc/resolv.conf (normally resolved(8) on
       127.0.0.1), then the kernel resolver as a last resort. Prints every
       address found.

EXAMPLES
       host google.com

SEE ALSO
       resolved(8), ping(1), ip(8)
